    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate proves that the vehicle meets emission standards. A valid, up‑to‑date PUC is required for all road transport.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The insurer’s certificate of coverage must be current and reflect the vehicle’s value. It should specify the policy number, coverage limits, and the insured party’s details.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Inland Bill of Lading (Bilty) issued by the India Board of Agricultural and Allied (IBA) confirms the shipment’s details, including vehicle make, model, weight, and destination. It also serves as a receipt for the consignor.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>Each of these documents must be presented to the transport operator, customs officials, and any relevant authorities en route. Failure to supply any of them can result in vehicle seizure, fines, or forced storage at the destination.</p>

<p>In addition to the standard paperwork, it is highly advisable to secure <strong>100% declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong>. This insurance covers the vehicle for the full market value in case of loss, theft, or damage during sea transport.</p>
<p>Marine transit insurance is separate from the standard road‑coverage policy and is specifically designed for the high risks associated with shipping. By declaring the vehicle’s full value, you ensure that any loss is compensated in full, protecting your investment and eliminating the financial uncertainty that can arise from under‑insured shipments.</p>

<p>In practice, the transport company will usually provide a template for the consignment bilty and will verify the self‑attested RC and PUC before loading the vehicle. Once the bilty is signed and the insurance certificate is attached, the shipment can proceed without interruption.</p>
<p>Always keep copies of all documents in both digital and hard‑copy form, and confirm that the transport operator has received and logged them. Proper documentation not only streamlines the process but also safeguards your vehicle throughout its journey across Curchorem Cacora’s roads and waterways.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


